@startuml AD-8
!include _style.iuml
title AD-8 (System level) — Onboard a Charge Point and first connection\nTrigger: Admin registers a new Charge Point serial\nUse cases: UC-ADM-03, UC-OPS-01, UC-INT-01, UC-INT-04, UC-OPS-02

|«person»\nAdmin|
|«person»\nOperator|
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
|«external system»\nCharge Point|
|«person»\nAdmin|
start
:Register the Charge Point\nserial in the registry;
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
if ( ) then ([serial already\nin the registry])
  :Reject duplicate serial;
  stop
else ([new serial])
  :Save serial;
endif
:ChargePoint\n&#91;registered&#93;]
|«person»\nOperator|
:Enter serial, choose own\nsite and connectors;
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
:Check site ownership\nand serial status;
if ( ) then ([site of another Operator, or serial\nnot registered or already onboarded])
  :Refuse with reason;
  stop
else ([valid])
endif
:Assign to site, create connectors,\nissue credential and show it once;
:ChargePoint\n&#91;awaiting_connection&#93;]
:Connector\n&#91;Unavailable&#93;]
|«person»\nOperator|
:Configure the Charge Point with\nplatform address and credential;
|«external system»\nCharge Point|
:Connect with credential\nand send boot report>
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
if ( ) then ([wrong credential])
  :Reject connection and log it\n(Charge Point stays awaiting);
  stop
else ([credential valid])
endif
:Accept boot and set\nheartbeat interval;
:ChargePoint\n&#91;in_service&#93;]
:Read capabilities (reservation\nsupport, battery-level reporting,\nfree-vend tag);
|«external system»\nCharge Point|
:Report each\nconnector's status>
|«software system»\nPowerMe Platform|
:Show connectors on the\nDriver map and dashboard;
:Connector\n&#91;Available&#93;]
|«person»\nOperator|
:See the Charge Point\nin service on the dashboard;
stop
@enduml
